s(DCIS)\\tDuctal carcinoma\n      insitu\\r\\nTisP|Tis(Paget)\\tPaget disease of the nipple NOT associated with invasive\n      carcinoma and/or carcinoma in situ (DCIS) in the underlying breast parenchyma.\n      Carcinomas in the breast parenchyma associated with Paget disease are categorized\n      based on the size and characteristics of the parenchymal disease, although the\n      presence of Paget disease should still be noted.\\r\\nT1a|T1a\\tTumor >1 mm but\n      ≤ 5 mm in greatest dimension (round any measurement > 1.0-1.9 mm to 2 mm)\\r\\nT1b|T1b\\tTumor\n      >5 mm but ≤ 10 mm in greatest dimension\\r\\nT1c|T1c\\tTumor >10 mm but ≤ 20 mm\n      in greatest dimension\\r\\nT2|T2\\tTumor > 20 mm but ≤ 50 mm in greastest dimension\\r\\nT3|T3\\tTumor\n      > 50 mm greastest dimension\\r\\nT4a|T4a\\tExtension to chest wall; invasion or\n      adherence to pectoralis muscle in the absence of invasion of chest wall structures\n      does not qualify as T4\\r\\nT4b|T4b\\tUlceration and/or ipsilateral macroscopic\n      satellite nodules and/or edema (including peau d’orange) of the skin that does\n      not meet the criteria for inflammatory carcinoma\\r\\nT4c|T4c\\tBoth T4a and T4b\n      are present\\r\\nT4d|T4d\\tInflammatory carcinoma\"\n- !ruby/struct:FIELDCOMPRESSION\n  attributes:\n    :id: F9885383153\n    :name: Patho N\n    :label: N @\n    :column_name: patho_n\n    :field_type: select_string\n    :style: width:600px\n    :lov_type: pair\n    :lov: \"cNx|cNx\\tRegional lymph nodes cannot be assessed\\r\\ncN0|cN0\\tNo regional\n      lymph node metastasis\\r\\ncN1|cN1\\tMetastases to movable ipsilateral level I,\n      II axillary lymph node(s)\\r\\ncNm|cN1mi\\tmicrometastases (approximately 200 cells,\n      larger than 0.2 mm, but none larger than 2.0 mm)\\r\\ncN2a|cN2a\\tMetastases in\n      ipsilateral level I, II axillary lymph nodes fixed to one another (matted) or\n      to other structures\\r\\ncN2b|cN2b\\tMetastases only in ipsilateral internal mammary\n      nodes in the absence of axillary lymph node metastases\\r\\ncN3a|cN3a\\tMetastasis\n      in ipsilateral infraclavicular lymph node(s)\\r\\ncN3b|cN3b\\tMetastasis in ipsilateral\n      internal mammary lymph node(s) and axillary lymph node(s)\\r\\ncN3c|cN3c\\tMetastasis\n      in ipsilateral supraclavicular lymph node(s)\\r\\npNx|pNx\\tRegional lymph nodes\n      cannot be assessed\\r\\npN0|pN0\\tNo regional lymph node metastasis identified\n      or ITCs only\\r\\npN0i|pN0(i+)\\tITCs only (malignant cells clusters no larger\n      than 0.2 mm) in regional lymph node(s)\\r\\npN0Mol|pN0(Mol+)\\tPositive molecular\n      findings by reverse transcriptase polymerase chain (RT-PCR); no ITCs detected\\r\\npNm|pN1mi\\tmicrometastases\n      (200 cells, larger than 0.2 mm, but none larger than 2.0 mm)\\r\\npN1a|pN1a\\tMetastases\n      in 1-3 axillary lymph nodes, at least one metastasis larger than 2.0 mm\\r\\npN1b|pN1b\\tMetastases\n      in ipsilateral internal mammary sentinel nodes, excluding ITCs\\r\\npN1c|pN1c\\tpN1a\n      and pN1b combined.\\r\\npN2a|pN2a\\tMetastases in 4-9 axillary lymph nodes (at\n      least one tumor deposit larger than 2.0 mm)\\r\\npN2b|pN2b\\tMetastases in clinically\n      detected internal mammary lymph nodes with or without microscopic confirmation;\n      with pathologically negative axillary nodes\\r\\npN3a|pN3a\\tMetastases in 10 or\n      more axillary lymph nodes (at least one tumor deposit greater than 2.0 mm);\n      or metastases to the infraclavicular (level lll axillary lymph) nodes\\r\\npN3b|pN3b\\tpN1a\n      or pN2a in the presence of c N2b (positive internal mammary nodes by imagint)\n      or pN2a in the presence of pN1b\\r\\npN3c|pN3c\\tMetastasis in ipsilateral supraclavicular\n      lymph nodes\"\n- !ruby/struct:FIELDCOMPRESSION\n  attributes:\n    :id: F0039222355\n    :name: Patho M\n    :label: M @\n    :column_name: patho_m\n    :field_type: select_string\n    :style: width:600px\n    :lov_type: pai